# Commands & setup

## Docker (local dev)
```bash
docker compose up -d --build   # build + start all services
docker compose logs -f api     # API logs
docker compose down            # stop
```

## Testing (Docker must run for integration)
```bash
APP_ENV=test uv run pytest                          # all
APP_ENV=test uv run pytest tests/unit               # unit
APP_ENV=test uv run pytest tests/integration        # integration
APP_ENV=test uv run pytest tests/integration/test_auth_login.py  # single file
APP_ENV=test uv run pytest -v                       # verbose
APP_ENV=test uv run pytest --cov                    # coverage (term)
APP_ENV=test uv run pytest --cov --cov-report=html  # HTML -> htmlcov/
```
Coverage config is in `.coveragerc` (line + branch, `source = app`), NOT `pyproject.toml`.
`pytest.ini` overrides `[tool.pytest.ini_options]`, so pytest settings in pyproject are ignored.
CI comments coverage on PRs; it does not gate.

## Lint / format (Ruff)
```bash
uv run ruff check .            # lint
uv run ruff check . --fix      # auto-fix (local only)
uv run ruff format .           # format (local only)
uv run ruff format --check .   # CI / handover check
```
Line length 120, target py311, ignores B008 (FastAPI `Depends()` defaults), excludes `migrations/`, `lib/`, `venv/`. CI is check-only (no `--fix`).

## Migrations (Alembic)
```bash
docker compose exec api alembic revision --autogenerate -m "Description"
docker compose exec api alembic upgrade head
```

## Environment
Copy `.env.example` to `.env.development` and `.env.test`; `APP_ENV` selects the file
(default `.env.development`, `test` for tests). Key vars: `POSTGRES_*`, `JWT_*`,
`GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` / `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET`, `MAIL_*`, `FRONTEND_URL`.
